Design ideas and code patterns derived from WinLinuxBridge include:
  - the Windows-initiated reverse SSH tunnel architecture (no inbound ports,
    no admin rights, no system installation on either side);
  - persistent job execution semantics (request-id dedup, three separated
    timeouts, bounded output with SHA-256 and byte-cursor reads, LOST state);
  - GDI-based screenshot capture with standard-library zlib PNG encoding;
  - tunnel failure diagnostics and exponential retry backoff;
  - the two-dedicated-key security model (restricted tunnel key + management key).

